=== PARITY (vs web DriveTelemetryWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (DriveTelemetrySource → DriveTelemetryModel):
    useVehicles, useDrives, useDriveTelemetry, useUnits, useTranslation, useThemeChartPalette.
    Production wires DriveTelemetrySource over the KMP DriveStore (drive list) + DriveTelemetryStore
    (selected drive samples) + the settings UnitStore; the view performs NO HTTP. No transport in the view.
  Projection → DriveTelemetryProjectionBuilder.build is a faithful port of the widget's useMemo work:
    latestDrive = max by startTs; chartData drops samples without a timestamp (timestamp ?? createdAt),
    converts speed SI m/s → display (convertSpeedFromSI), carries power (kW pass-through), battery =
    batteryLevel ?? soc, elevation (m), sorted ascending; stats = Distance (convertDistanceFromSI, 1dp),
    Duration (durationS/60 int, "min"), Efficiency (energyUsedWh / displayDistance, 0dp) ONLY when
    energyUsedWh != null && distanceM > 0 (Wh/km|Wh/mi). Verified by executed XCTest (13) + harness (21).
  Composition → WidgetShell chrome (waveform icon + "Drive Telemetry" title + freshness chip + refresh +
    optional Open) · stat header (Distance / Duration / Efficiency + wide startAddress badge) · the chart ·
    legend (Speed / Power (kW) / Battery % / +Elevation when wide). Recharts ComposedChart → Swift Charts:
    speed LineMark (cyan, left), battery dashed LineMark (amber/green, left), elevation AreaMark (muted,
    left, wide only), power AreaMark+LineMark (right axis). The single Swift Charts Y scale renders the
    web's dual axes faithfully via DriveTelemetryChartScale (power ↔ left plotting space), so the right
    power axis lines up with the left series, exactly as the web's two YAxis do.
  Shared components → reuses the REAL apps/apple library compiled in GATE [1]/[2]: Color.TS, Font.TS,
    TSSpacing, TSRadius (tokens), chart-series color tokens, TSSkeleton (loading), ContentUnavailableView
    (empty / no-telemetry). Recharts→Swift Charts; Leaflet→none (web uses no map). Color tokens map the
    web series: speed→chartSeriesSpeed, power→chartSeriesPower, battery→chartSeriesBattery,
    elevation #9ca3af→textMuted.
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No recent drives" + waveform) when no drive ·
    inner "No telemetry for this drive" when a drive has no samples · error (retry) · stale (chip + banner,
    cached chart stays) · offline (chip + banner, cached chart) · content. Model phase resolution keeps
    cached content visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell.
  i18n → all 11 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
